1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
<font color="#20e020">Cleaned and corrected by Lunar Team</font>

2
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,704
Thank god. You're here.

3
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:40,706
There was screaming, then gunshots.

4
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:43,000
Upstairs in room 222.

5
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:47,379
The one... The one on the right.

6
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,048
Right there.

7
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:55,471
Police! Open the door.

8
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:00,976
Come on. Open up.

9
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,964
Copy that.

10
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:41,183
Glad you could make it.

11
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:46,480
We have young female,
Patrice Matigan and Joseph Purcell...

12
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:49,691
...who was gonna be the star witness
in California v. Carris...

13
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:52,194
...which was
one of the attorney general's...

14
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:55,405
...favorite upcoming narcotics cases.

15
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,243
State's witness
and no police protection?

16
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,702
Davis PD had it covered.

17
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,372
That is, until Purcell went AWOL
a few weeks ago.

18
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:06,041
Didn't wanna testify, I guess.

19
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:09,128
With Purcell dead,
the case against Carris dies too.

20
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:10,462
He walks.

21
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,464
So obviously, guys...

22
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:15,467
...for all of our sakes,
this is a must-close.

23
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,388
Davis PD is still running
the Carris case...

24
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,014
...so we have to work with them.

25
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:22,224
Don't freeze them out.

26
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:24,560
Who is Carris
and where is he or she right now?

27
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,396
Rick Carris is the man to know
in the Davis meth business.

28
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:31,567
He was, uh, busted a month ago
after a big, expensive operation.

29
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:35,112
He's out and about
on a $2 million bond.

30
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:38,157
Purcell here is one of his top
street captains.

31
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,412
Look at that. Ha-ha-ha.

32
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:47,708
This fool is state's witness against
the biggest cocaine dealer in the county...

33
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:49,960
...and he's dealing the drug
out of his room.

34
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:53,505
Like Carris wouldn't hear about that.
Must have had a death wish.

35
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,217
Looks like a couple of ounces.

36
00:02:57,385 --> 00:02:58,510
It's not cocaine.

37
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:02,764
It's powdered milk.

38
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:05,142
Yes, that's often used
to cut the product.

39
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,351
Jane?

40
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:18,405
- What are you looking for?
- The girl had her keys in her hand.

41
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:20,782
She was only planning on stopping by.

42
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,631
Oh, no.

43
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,175
Hello.

44
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,010
Baby.

45
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,970
Hello.

46
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,150
So, what happens to her?

47
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:58,403
Social Services have foster moms
that specialize in babies.

48
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:01,240
We'll take care of her until
we can find Patrice's family.

49
00:04:01,407 --> 00:04:02,616
If she has a family.

50
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,868
Social Services. I'm here for Kaylee.

51
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:07,204
Hi.

52
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:10,958
Bye.

53
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:18,006
Lisbon, Jane, Van Pelt.

54
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:22,135
Detectives Blakely and Preciado,
Davis Homicide.

55
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:25,013
They will be your liaisons with Davis PD

56
00:04:25,181 --> 00:04:29,768
I speak for myself and your chief
when I urge you all to work harmoniously.

57
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:32,145
That means play nice.

58
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:33,689
Keep me posted.

59
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,232
Hi.

60
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,609
So your name's Blakely?

61
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:40,529
- First responder was a Blakely.
- That's my son.

62
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:43,198
Poor kid. First time rolling up on a body.

63
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,659
- Puked his guts up later.
- He'll be okay.

64
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:48,078
Listen, uh, just so we're clear.

65
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:54,126
Now, you can call us liaisons if you like,
but this is still a Davis PD case.

66
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,920
Our Narcotics Unit's been trying
to bust Rick Carris for years.

67
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:59,548
We appreciate your position.

68
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,634
Have you checked the liquor store
for surveillance cameras?

69
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:04,886
Not yet. We're still questioning the guests.

70
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,054
I'll get on it.

71
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:09,558
I got a dumb question, how come
you guys let Joe Purcell slip away?

72
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:12,769
- Stuff happens, right?
- Yeah. Stuff happens.

73
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:15,772
Yeah, when we bring in Rick Carris,
we'll give you a call.

74
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,025
You're confident it was Carris
who did this?

75
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:21,236
Purcell seems like the type of man
who had quite a few enemies.

76
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,572
Yeah. We're confident.

77
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,408
What if Purcell wasn't the target?
What if the girl was?

78
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:29,119
- What makes you think that?
- What makes you think she wasn't?

79
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:32,581
Either way, she's the place to start
with the investigation.

80
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:36,335
She was here for a moment so the shooter
came in as soon as she arrived.

81
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:39,004
Which suggests
that he or they followed her here.

82
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:43,216
So we'll retrace her steps.
What's Patrice Matigan's current address?

83
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:44,676
We don't know.

84
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:48,805
We checked the address on her license.
She hasn't lived here for several months.

85
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:51,433
You're making this more difficult
than it needs to be.

86
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:54,144
We know who done it.
This was a hit ordered by Carris.

87
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:56,104
If he's in town, we'll round him up.

88
00:05:56,272 --> 00:06:00,275
You guys relax. See the sights.
We'll call you when there's any news.

89
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,905
When are you gonna learn to cool it
without being told?

90
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:07,949
Oh, come on, they pissed you off too,
the sexist pigs.

91
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:09,159
They were.

92
00:06:10,286 --> 00:06:11,370
I just said they were.

93
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:13,914
You were saying it ironically.

94
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:17,417
Here. There were a couple
of issues of that in her car.

95
00:06:18,294 --> 00:06:21,630
"Fifty Fresh and Floral Ideas
for a Spring Wedding"?

96
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,424
Why on earth would
Patrice Matigan have this?

97
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,218
Mailing address.

98
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:31,765
Lacey Wells. 65758 Rancho Highway.
Let's go.

99
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:41,650
Lacey Wells?

100
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,694
- You the cops?
- Yeah, CBI.

101
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,448
- What's the problem?
- Do you know Patrice Matigan?

102
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,118
She lives here.

103
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:53,912
What about her? And where is she?

104
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,705
She was murdered this morning.

105
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:59,376
Oh, my God.

106
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,756
How long have you known Patrice?

107
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:07,426
Couple of years, like that.

108
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:09,803
And she's lived here with you
for how long?

109
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,430
Since Joe got busted.

110
00:07:12,181 --> 00:07:13,306
Two, three months.

111
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,143
She couldn't stay with him
the way he lives.

112
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,311
Son of a bitch.

113
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:21,148
No... I knew he'd get her into trouble.

114
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,942
Can you think of anybody
who would've wanted to kill him?

115
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:26,778
Aside from Rick Carris
and any of his crew?

116
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,280
Sure.

117
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,656
Lots of people.

118
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:31,908
Could you tell us
what happened last night?

119
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:34,995
Joe called her really late.

120
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:38,123
He's mad hungry, but he's paranoid.

121
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:42,127
Won't leave his room.
Thinks Rick Carris' boys are everywhere.

122
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:45,464
Begs her to bring him some food.

123
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:49,718
Which she does, like a fool.

124
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,721
And that's...

125
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:55,765
That's the last I saw of her and Kaylee.

126
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:00,979
Why would she take Kaylee out
with her in the middle of the night?

127
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,898
Couldn't you have babysat for her?

128
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,651
I had been drinking.

129
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:10,197
And she didn't wanna leave Kaylee
with me.

130
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,491
She had her flaws...

131
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,367
...but she was a good mom.

132
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:17,412
I mean, that kid is always clean...

133
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,831
...and dry and she's smiling.

134
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,418
I mean, look at how she keeps this place.

135
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:26,796
Yeah, it's nice. How did she pay the rent?

136
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:29,758
Oh, she always has money
when she needs it.

137
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,302
You know, her and me got busted
this last Christmas.

138
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:35,055
And she came up with like 10 grand
to front the bail.

139
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,848
And even more for the lawyer.

140
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:41,561
We were busted with a whole ounce
of meth and she made that crap disappear.

141
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:44,147
- She was into meth?
- No.

142
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,649
No.

143
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:46,900
No, it was my drugs.

144
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:52,447
But it was in her car so, you know.

145
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:55,825
Did you ask how she got the money
to pay for the lawyer?

146
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,494
She wasn't the hooker type...

147
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:01,206
...so I just figured she had
a rich boyfriend hidden somewhere.

148
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,960
You know, couple of times,
a dude would come by and not come in.

149
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:10,465
And she'd go for a ride and then
she had cash when she came back.

150
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:11,800
What did he look like?

151
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:15,387
He was like a skinny, tough guy.

152
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:18,014
Dark hair. And drove a blue car.

153
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,810
Excuse me.

154
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:24,813
- Always goes off.
- Lisbon.

155
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,815
Just got a call from
Sacramento Homicide.

156
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,733
Snitch gave them a location
on Carris.

157
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:31,194
He's in Boonville,
halfway between here and Davis.

158
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:33,071
Get an entry team. We're on our way.

159
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:35,199
- Should I tell Blakely and Preciado?
- Of course.

160
00:09:35,324 --> 00:09:39,452
Davis PD are our partners on this.
Hold off on going in until I get there.

161
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,540
Thank you, Lacey.

162
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:47,419
Yeah. Hey, uh, listen,
Social Services, they're...

163
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,088
They're not gonna bring Kaylee
back here, are they?

164
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,215
- No.
- I love her and all...

165
00:09:52,383 --> 00:09:54,426
...but I'm not... I couldn't...

166
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:57,137
Don't worry. They're not
gonna bring her back here, okay?

167
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,514
She goes somewhere okay though, right?

168
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:03,810
- I mean, they'll take care of her good?
- Yes. They try.

169
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:06,688
She's a good kid, so...

170
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,113
Hey. Where you going?

171
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:17,616
To make the bust. What do you think?
Cover the back.

172
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:19,784
- Wait.
- What?

173
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:22,203
You guys wanna help
or you're gonna stand there?

174
00:10:22,371 --> 00:10:24,748
Come on, guys, play nice.
This is a joint operation.

175
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:26,541
We go in when our boss
and team get here.

176
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:29,002
Uh-uh, this is our arrest.
Always has been.

177
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:31,129
And we got no time
to wait for your mommy.

178
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:35,175
There's always time. Let's do this right.
Go in too quickly, someone will get hurt.

179
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:37,802
This is real police work, sonny.
People get hurt.

180
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,805
- Go push some paper.
- Real police work?

181
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:42,974
You mean like protecting
a state's witness?

182
00:10:43,934 --> 00:10:46,061
Hey, hey, walk away. Walk away.
Look at me.

183
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:48,813
We told them not to.
This goes south, it's their necks.

184
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:52,108
We don't wanna be involved
in any way. Be smart. Just let it go.

185
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,282
What's going on?
What are they doing?

186
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,242
They wouldn't wait for the entry team.

187
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:04,287
- We tried to talk to them, wouldn't listen.
- They're out for blood.

188
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:27,102
Don't move, Carris, hands up.

189
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,187
He's running.

190
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:47,706
- Get on your knees right now.
- Let me see your hands.

191
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,834
That's our bust. Hand him over.

192
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:54,295
The hell we will. Walk away.

193
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:56,965
Hey, calm down.

194
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:12,272
Yes, we get it.

195
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:15,316
You're very calm and in control, Rick...

196
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:18,987
...for a man being questioned
in a double murder investigation.

197
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:20,196
I didn't do this thing.

198
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:23,241
Although I've been sat in this
freaking chair so many times...

199
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,619
- ...this is kind of restful.
- That's right, isn't it? Many times.

200
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:30,290
Assault.

201
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,167
Possession. Intent to distribute.

202
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:35,378
This trafficking case coming up,
that's three and out for you?

203
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:38,298
- You get nailed, you're in for life.
- That's a long time.

204
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:40,133
All on the testimony of Joe Purcell.

205
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:44,095
Look, it's no secret Joe Purcell's death
was a huge boon for me, man...

206
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,097
...come on, it was huge.

207
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:49,142
I gotta confess,
I was really starting to feel...

208
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:52,353
...that life sentence breathing
down my neck. But you know what?

209
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:54,022
I got angels, man.

210
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,191
I got fierce angels on my shoulders.

211
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:58,318
Are you a man of your word, Rick?

212
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,528
- I am.
- You do what you say you'll do.

213
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,864
Look, I know where this is going.

214
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:05,200
This is from Purcell's answering machine.

215
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:08,161
Hey, Joe, you're a dead man. Dead.

216
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:11,206
I'm gonna do you my own self.
I'm gonna look you in the eye...

217
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,708
...cut your heart out,
shove it down your throat...

218
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,210
That is you, isn't it?

219
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:19,547
- Hyperbole is lost on some people.
- We think you kept your word, Rick.

220
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:22,008
You found Patrice,
followed her to the motel.

221
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:25,428
You killed him and that young girl
just to stay out of prison.

222
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:27,680
- Just like you said you would.
- No, I said...

223
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:30,350
...I was gonna cut his heart out
and feed it to him.

224
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:32,352
Poetic license.

225
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,938
No, if I'd have found him,
I would have kept my word.

226
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:37,690
I was looking for him.
That's how you know it wasn't me.

227
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:40,735
I wouldn't have cut his heart out,
but I would've cut him.

228
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:42,904
I mean, I got a reputation to consider.

229
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,531
Where were you last night?

230
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,324
A bar I own. Del's Tavern.

231
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,951
Until when?

232
00:13:48,577 --> 00:13:50,078
I don't know, 11:30 maybe.

233
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:53,164
- Anyone with you?
- Oh, yeah.

234
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,208
- Sasha.
- Sasha?

235
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:56,543
Sasha have a second name?

236
00:13:58,087 --> 00:13:59,587
Sasha, the cocktail waitress.

237
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:02,799
One young lady in your employ.
That's not much of an alibi.

238
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,592
It's not much of a case, man.

239
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,428
You got no murder weapon
and you got no witnesses.

240
00:14:07,596 --> 00:14:09,639
So you can kiss my ass.

241
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:12,684
Unless you wanna get a sun lamp in here
and a couple of beers.

242
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:17,063
I'll be happy to kick back and listen
to you guys waste your freaking time.

243
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,899
I guess I'll just hand you over
to the Davis PD

244
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,610
They're very anxious to talk to you.

245
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:27,073
All right, whatever.
I wanna talk to my lawyer now, please.

246
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,242
Okay. So we're done here.

247
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:34,789
Food's here.

248
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:39,043
- Hawaiian?
- Yeah.

249
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:40,837
Cho hates pineapple.

250
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,964
Well, he can take it off, can't he?

251
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:44,632
Yeah, I guess.

252
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,135
I don't complain
when he and Rigsby order Mexican.

253
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:51,472
- What is it you don't like about Mexican?
- Cilantro. I can't stand it.

254
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,057
But I don't make a fuss.

255
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:54,976
No, you don't, do you? Why is that?

256
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:59,272
Sometimes you have to go along
to get along.

257
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:04,319
It's nice to be nice. But if you wanna get
ahead, sometimes you have to be a bitch.

258
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:07,405
- I know you know how.
- Gee, thanks.

259
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:10,575
It's all about the balance, Grace.
Yin, yang.

260
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,493
Nice, bitch.

261
00:15:12,661 --> 00:15:16,331
Little bit of bitch inside the nice.
Little bit of nice inside the bitch.

262
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:19,667
- Yeah, I'll work on that.
- Keep them guessing.

263
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,590
There's pineapple on it.

264
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:29,510
- You can take it off.
- I'll know it's been there.

265
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,931
So Carris was at Del's Tavern.

266
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:36,976
Sasha, the cocktail waitress says she was
with him at his residence at 12:45 a.m...

267
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:38,686
...when the shootings took place.

268
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:42,357
She's confident about the time because
they were having sex with the TV on.

269
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:45,044
The Scottish guy talking
to that actress who married the singer.

270
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:48,112
Carris would've got someone else
do the dirty work anyway.

271
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:51,157
He was boasting when he said
he was gonna rip Purcell's heart.

272
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:54,035
- He's a drug dealer, not an Aztec.
- That's good.

273
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:58,039
Not an Aztec. You're right.
Carris isn't responsible for these murders.

274
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,625
- Why not?
- He told you himself. It's not his style.

275
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:03,127
He wouldn't have the patience
to follow Patrice...

276
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:04,796
...until she led him to Purcell.

277
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:08,049
If he'd found her, he would've
hurt her until she gave Purcell up.

278
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:10,718
For the sake of argument,
let's assume you're right.

279
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:13,554
Yes, and I'm saying
maybe Patrice Matigan was the target.

280
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:15,322
That's the second time you've said that.

281
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:19,477
Well, Patrice, she was an attractive,
young woman, but didn't work...

282
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,397
...and had a regular supply of money
from somewhere.

283
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:24,732
- Boyfriend.
- And was able to make...

284
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:27,026
...a very serious drug charge disappear.

285
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:28,434
- Cop boyfriend.
- Skinny cop...

286
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:32,073
...with dark hair that drives a blue car,
if you listen to Lacey.

287
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:34,242
Detective Preciado is skinny
with dark hair.

288
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,868
He had crossed my mind.

289
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:38,746
And a hot-tempered man,
as we now know.

290
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:41,082
Who probably carries what, a .38?

291
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,126
- Yeah. Yeah. I think he does.
- Yeah.

292
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:46,087
- Joe and Patrice were shot with a .38.
- Yes, they were.

293
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,588
Slow down. What's his motive?

294
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:49,090
A simple crime of passion.

295
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:52,176
He comes upon the woman he loves
with another man. Kills them.

296
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:55,722
He couldn't have been that surprised.
She had Joe Purcell's baby.

297
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,140
How is she?

298
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:59,767
- The baby.
- Uh, fine, I guess.

299
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:01,227
I mean, she's a baby.

300
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,187
Keep them warm and fed, they're happy.

301
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:05,148
Let's go have a chat with Preciado.

302
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:07,775
We're already in hot water
with the Davis PD

303
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:10,445
We need to be sure we're right.

304
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:13,614
- Find out the facts and then act.
- Yes, boss.

305
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:17,118
Let's see if Patrice really did dodge
a possession charge at Christmas...

306
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,455
...and let's make sure the story
about the accident money is bogus.

307
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:23,583
Then we'll go to Lacey
and we'll show her pictures.

308
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,627
If she ID's Preciado as the man she saw...

309
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:31,132
...and if Preciado drives a blue car
and if he carries a .38...

310
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,925
...we'll go and we'll talk to him.

311
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:35,219
Preciado owns a blue car.

312
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,348
May I have your salad?

313
00:17:57,826 --> 00:18:01,788
Oh, Gladys Knight and the Pips.

314
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:03,206
You brought our prisoner back?

315
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:07,210
Detective Preciado, we need
to sit down with you for a while.

316
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:09,504
- We have a few questions for you.
- What questions?

317
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:11,923
That's a .38 you carry, isn't it?

318
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:15,134
You trying to say it was me?

319
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:18,179
You sons of bitches.
Where the hell do you get the...?

320
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:21,015
- Steve. Cool it. Let me handle this.
- No. This one's mine.

321
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:23,351
Where do you get the nerve
to come in my town...

322
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:26,229
...talking to me like that?
What weapon do I carry?

323
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:28,356
Kiss my ass.

324
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,858
California State Constitution.

325
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,944
We've come to you out here
out of respect.

326
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:35,363
We could have found you
in the station and made a fuss.

327
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:38,574
- You should be glad you didn't.
- You should be glad we didn't.

328
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:41,786
You have nothing on me.

329
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:43,913
We can put you with Patrice.

330
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:45,873
Her roommate ID'd you from a photo.

331
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:48,376
Have a talk with us.
Clear up a couple of things.

332
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:50,419
- No big deal.
- What couple of things?

333
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:52,088
This doesn't concern you, detective.

334
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:55,049
- Excuse me, he's my partner.
- Leave it alone, Dale.

335
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:57,051
Just leave it. I can handle this.

336
00:18:57,553 --> 00:18:59,220
Let's go.

337
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:04,016
Hi.

338
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:10,815
Mm. Mm.

339
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,609
- Good to meet you again.
- Hey.

340
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:16,529
What's the matter with him?

341
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,573
How well do you know Patrice Matigan?

342
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:20,950
Let's not screw around.
Tell me what you have.

343
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:23,411
- Cop to cop.
- Cop to cop?

344
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:25,163
We know you were giving her money.

345
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:27,498
Know she got off of a meth bust
last Christmas.

346
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:30,835
Evidence was lost, right?
From the Davis PD lockup.

347
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:33,421
- Happens.
- We figure you took it.

348
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:34,839
That's what you figure?

349
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:38,426
Yes. We could dig in and prove it
but I don't wanna spend time doing that.

350
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,511
I'd rather just talk straight with you.

351
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:43,931
Avoid dragging other good cops
into this mess, right?

352
00:19:44,099 --> 00:19:45,141
Go on.

353
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:49,770
We figure you and Patrice
were having a sexual relationship.

354
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:53,941
She was...

355
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:56,986
She was a confidential informant.

356
00:19:57,154 --> 00:20:00,031
We considered that.
But then she'd be on file, right?

357
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,700
And you would've put in
for the money as a CI expense.

358
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:05,161
But you didn't do that, did you?

359
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:07,997
Why? My guess,
because you're an honest man.

360
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,624
Yeah. Sure.

361
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,292
Okay.

362
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:13,502
I was banging her. So what?

363
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:17,256
Did you know she was in a relationship
with your missing witness?

364
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:20,468
We had a business relationship.
I paid her for sex.

365
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:23,346
I didn't know or care
what she did when I wasn't there.

366
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,681
You paid her a lot of money. A lot.

367
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:29,769
A good-looking man like you?
There had to have been more to it than that.

368
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:32,688
- Did she have something on you?
- She was punctual and clean.

369
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,482
Didn't say much. I like that in a woman.

370
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,860
Did you know your man,
Joe Purcell, was the father of her child?

371
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:39,195
No.

372
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:42,073
A lowlife, junkie dealer with your woman.

373
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,407
How'd that make you feel?

374
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:45,910
Couldn't care less.

375
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:51,624
Do you, uh,
want the rest of my sandwich?

376
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:52,959
- I can't finish it.
- What?

377
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:55,336
It's a good sandwich, try it.
Good sandwich.

378
00:20:57,756 --> 00:20:59,006
What is wrong with him?

379
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:02,802
Where were you at 12:45 a.m.
Monday morning?

380
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,304
I was at my partner's.

381
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:09,934
We watched the game, I was too drunk
to drive, so I slept on the couch.

382
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:12,603
- At Blakely's? Just you and him?
- And his wife.

383
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:15,398
Do you have your weapon on you?

384
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:18,025
Yes, I do.

385
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:22,446
Mind if we borrow it for a while?
Have Ballistics take a look at it?

386
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:27,326
I don't want to have to make this official,
talk to a judge or anything.

387
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:30,746
Once we do that,
the cat's out of the bag for good.

388
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:34,458
If you're clean on this,
here's the way to prove it.

389
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:43,384
- Is this the only .38 in your possession?
- Yes, it is.

390
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,177
If you try to hold my hand again...

391
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:48,264
...I'm gonna tear your arm off
and beat you unconscious with it.

392
00:21:48,432 --> 00:21:50,891
- Get me?
- Got you.

393
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:54,979
- Well?
- It's funny what bad liars cops are.

394
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:58,024
They're not used to concealing themselves
under questioning.

395
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:00,818
I'm a cop, I lie to you all the time,
you never catch it.

396
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:03,404
Sorry to burst your bubble,
but you're translucent.

397
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:05,031
I always know when you're lying.

398
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:08,868
Sometimes I let you think you've
fooled me just so you don't feel bad.

399
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:10,453
Name one time.

400
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:14,415
Ahem, last Thanksgiving, you said you were
going back East to your brother's house.

401
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,834
You actually planned
three days at home alone...

402
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,003
...to watch old movies and eat ice cream.

403
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:21,464
Okay, so that's one time.

404
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:28,971
- What about Preciado?
- His stressed pulse rate was thready.

405
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:30,431
Dishonest.

406
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:31,807
Thready?

407
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:36,354
Hard to describe pulses, dishonest pulse
feels different to an indignant pulse.

408
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:39,190
In this case, hard to say
what he's lying about exactly.

409
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:42,193
But he was signaling deception
from first to last.

410
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:44,612
There's something off.
Where're we going?

411
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:47,073
- To the zoo. They have new tiger cubs.
- Oh.

412
00:22:47,574 --> 00:22:49,325
- Liar.
- Oh, very good.

413
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:52,495
- I'm gonna speak with Blakely.
- Blakely's not gonna tell you anything.

414
00:22:52,662 --> 00:22:55,122
No, Blakely's old school.
He'll back his partner.

415
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:57,083
But his wife might be less steadfast.

416
00:22:57,250 --> 00:23:00,836
I'll keep the husband in the office
while you go and talk to the wife.

417
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,297
Sweet.

418
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:22,358
- What is it?
- Patrick Jane. CBI.

419
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:25,653
- Yeah, what is it?
- I'd like to speak with Katherine Blakely.

420
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:28,322
Sam? Officer Sam Blakely?

421
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:32,868
Yeah, uh, now isn't very convenient.
You should call and arrange something.

422
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:35,079
Yes, I was just passing by.

423
00:23:35,247 --> 00:23:37,998
That's a shame, Sam.
I really do need to speak to her.

424
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:40,167
Who is it, Sam?

425
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:42,753
CBI, ma'am. Murder investigation.

426
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:45,548
- Murder investigation?
- The Purcell-Matigan killings?

427
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:48,759
- That couple I found.
- Oh, my Lord, yes.

428
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:52,513
Terrible thing. That poor little baby.

429
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:54,723
- Well, I'll leave you to it then.
- No, ma'am.

430
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:58,310
It's you that I wish to speak with.

431
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:03,315
I am so proud of my two policemen.

432
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:07,361
There are three generations of Davis Law
Enforcement in this family. Three.

433
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:10,698
When people see
the Blakely name in Davis...

434
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:14,869
- ...they know that it stands for something.
- Cripe's sakes, Ma. It's enough.

435
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:17,371
Oh, he hates me bragging on him.

436
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:22,501
So tell me, why on earth do you
wanna ask me about these killings?

437
00:24:22,669 --> 00:24:25,880
Officer Blakely,
could we have a moment alone, please?

438
00:24:26,965 --> 00:24:28,632
It's okay.

439
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:31,385
It's kind of confidential stuff, ma'am.

440
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:34,054
Go on, Sam.

441
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:37,683
I don't think I should, Mom.
Dad wouldn't like it.

442
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:42,396
Well, you're not your dad.
Just give us a moment.

443
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,356
Go on.

444
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:56,911
Mm.

445
00:25:00,248 --> 00:25:05,044
Sam was so upset that night.
It was his first time coming up on a killing.

446
00:25:05,212 --> 00:25:06,420
Poor thing.

447
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:10,007
Now, I remember
the first time Dale caught a bad call.

448
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:14,178
We were newlyweds
and he came home and he actually cried.

449
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:15,888
Tried to hide it.

450
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:21,185
But I told him and I told Sam
that there is no shame in feeling sad.

451
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:23,103
There isn't.

452
00:25:23,438 --> 00:25:25,606
You've experienced the same thing,
no doubt.

453
00:25:26,274 --> 00:25:28,150
Death is part of the job.

454
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:30,110
Yes, yes, it is.

455
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,197
Sorry. Rambling.

456
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:36,158
What did you wanna talk to me about,
Mr. Jane?

457
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:38,702
Ma'am, your husband's partner,
Detective Preciado...

458
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:40,746
...is a person of interest in the case.

459
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:43,582
Steve? No.

460
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:45,876
He said that he was here at your house...

461
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:48,504
...sleeping on your couch
at the time of the murders.

462
00:25:48,672 --> 00:25:50,714
That was 12:45 a.m. Monday morning.

463
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:54,176
- Was he here?
- Yes, yes, he was.

464
00:25:54,344 --> 00:25:55,678
He stayed the night.

465
00:25:55,845 --> 00:26:00,599
Why would you be interested in Steve?
He's such a straight arrow.

466
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:04,812
He said that he was having an affair
with Patrice Matigan.

467
00:26:07,482 --> 00:26:10,067
- Steve Preciado?
- Yes.

468
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,861
- Why not?
- I don't know.

469
00:26:13,029 --> 00:26:14,572
It just doesn't seem likely.

470
00:26:16,992 --> 00:26:18,617
Katherine, you're hiding something.

471
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:24,290
This is a state investigation.
You're obligated to tell me the truth.

472
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:29,461
You have to promise you will not say
it was me who spoke of it.

473
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:30,796
I won't tell a soul.

474
00:26:31,548 --> 00:26:34,592
Well, Dale says that Steve has a problem.

475
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:37,803
You know, down there.

476
00:26:38,346 --> 00:26:40,764
Down there, oh.

477
00:26:42,058 --> 00:26:44,518
- There's pills for that now.
- Yes.

478
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:49,315
No, he's a hopeless case, apparently.

479
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:52,192
Well, that's strange.

480
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:55,279
That's very strange,
because he's the one that told us...

481
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,323
...he was having an affair with Patrice.

482
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:58,699
No, well, knowing Steve...

483
00:26:58,867 --> 00:27:01,619
...I'm sure he was lying
to protect his machismo...

484
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:04,496
...or protecting someone else...

485
00:27:10,545 --> 00:27:13,172
Oh, I'm so sorry. How stupid of me.

486
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:14,506
No, it's...

487
00:27:14,674 --> 00:27:16,884
- What happened?
- Nothing. Uh.

488
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,469
It's just a little accident.

489
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:20,638
What did you say to her?
Huh? What have you done?

490
00:27:20,805 --> 00:27:22,139
He's done nothing.

491
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:25,017
- Your father...
- My father what? What did you tell her?

492
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:28,854
You knew.

493
00:27:29,022 --> 00:27:31,732
You knew that's who she was.

494
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:36,737
That's why the two of you have been
whispering in corners and acting so strange.

495
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:39,239
No, Ma, you got it all wrong.

496
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:41,075
You don't understand.

497
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:43,786
Dad wasn't having an affair.

498
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:57,633
- Dad, Mom thinks that...
- What, Sam? What do I think?

499
00:27:57,801 --> 00:28:02,304
You swore on his life. You swore on your
son's life you would never betray me again.

500
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:05,307
Come inside. I'm gonna tell you
the truth but not out here.

501
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:07,393
Oh, no, not out here.
You're Dale Blakely.

502
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:10,020
- You're one of the good guys.
- Get in the house now.

503
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:11,814
Detective Blakely...

504
00:28:13,692 --> 00:28:15,192
- Shut your mouth.
- You okay?

505
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:16,443
Assault. Assault.

506
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:22,074
- I'd rethink this new technique of yours.
- Yeah. Yeah, I can't disagree.

507
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:44,722
Now we're arresting them. Hooray.

508
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:47,349
He assaulted Jane.
And he looks good for the murders.

509
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:50,728
Before you charge a cop with murder,
he better look better than good.

510
00:28:50,895 --> 00:28:52,813
- He better look like the Mona Lisa.
- Yes...

511
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:55,899
Because if you're wrong,
we will have no murder suspect.

512
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:58,986
The attorney general will have
no narcotics case against Carris.

513
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:02,322
And we will have wrongly arrested
a distinguished veteran officer...

514
00:29:02,490 --> 00:29:04,366
...in his home jurisdiction.

515
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:06,243
Yes, boss.

516
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:09,955
What was the nature
of your relationship with Patrice Matigan?

517
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:11,457
I was helping her out.

518
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:14,835
Helping with close to a thousand bucks
a month. That's a lot of help.

519
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:18,422
- What did she give you in return?
- Nothing.

520
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:21,884
Okay. What story did you tell
your wife about the money?

521
00:29:23,970 --> 00:29:26,555
- I got nothing to say.
- How were you making ends meet?

522
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:29,516
Did you maybe take
a little drug money now and again?

523
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:33,020
I never took a penny. Not a damn penny.

524
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:36,398
If Patrice started asking you for more,
you'd have been hard-pressed?

525
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:38,358
Get me a lawyer.

526
00:29:38,651 --> 00:29:40,277
I'll set that up for you.

527
00:29:41,863 --> 00:29:43,947
Oh, where's your service revolver?

528
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:46,116
Agent Rigsby tells me
you didn't have it with you.

529
00:29:46,284 --> 00:29:48,035
- It was stolen.
- Yeah?

530
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:49,328
Yeah. From my car.

531
00:29:49,496 --> 00:29:53,040
Okay. It's no problem. It happens.

532
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:55,626
- A .38, was it?
- That's right.

533
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:58,253
I'll get you that lawyer.

534
00:30:01,716 --> 00:30:03,091
He's not gonna talk.

535
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:04,885
Poor soul.

536
00:30:05,053 --> 00:30:08,222
- He made his bed. He can lie in it.
- I never understood that one.

537
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:11,517
Because someone makes their bed,
why do they have to lie in it?

538
00:30:11,684 --> 00:30:13,769
What's to stop them
from lying in another bed?

539
00:30:13,937 --> 00:30:16,730
Or on the floor for that matter?

540
00:30:17,857 --> 00:30:19,733
Sam Blakely's here.

541
00:30:20,985 --> 00:30:23,070
Come on.

542
00:30:26,282 --> 00:30:28,075
Okay, Mr. Carris. You're free to go.

543
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:30,786
No, I wasn't gonna go anywhere anyways.

544
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:33,831
No, I can hang out here.

545
00:30:35,166 --> 00:30:36,917
Officer Blakely, thanks for coming.

546
00:30:37,085 --> 00:30:39,169
I got no choice.
You got my father locked up.

547
00:30:39,337 --> 00:30:41,672
- Is your mother okay?
- Don't worry about my mother.

548
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,549
- My father's innocent.
- We know that.

549
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:45,092
You people are making a big...

550
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:47,135
- What?
- We know your father didn't do it.

551
00:30:53,393 --> 00:30:56,895
This is from the security cameras
of the liquor store in front of the motel.

552
00:30:57,063 --> 00:31:00,065
- We finally got to look at it today.
- This is at 12:40 a.m.

553
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:03,861
That's Patrice Matigan's car arriving.

554
00:31:06,656 --> 00:31:09,575
And that is Rick Carris' man.

555
00:31:10,159 --> 00:31:14,204
We misjudged Carris.
He found Patrice, had a man follow her.

556
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:16,707
His license plate.
Can you make that bigger?

557
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:18,709
Yes, we can.

558
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,170
We know who it is.

559
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:25,632
- A thug that works for Carris named Q-Tip.
- Now, get this.

560
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:27,843
Carris says Q-Tip didn't kill them.

561
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:30,304
Q-Tip went to kill Joe,
but he got there too late.

562
00:31:30,471 --> 00:31:32,139
Someone else got to him first.

563
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:33,891
That's got to be a bunch of bull.

564
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:37,603
Carris says his man Q-Tip actually saw
the real killer.

565
00:31:37,770 --> 00:31:38,937
Saw the whole thing.

566
00:31:39,105 --> 00:31:40,981
So Carris is offering us a deal.

567
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:46,528
If we let him out, his man Q-Tip will tell us
exactly what he saw, ID the real killer.

568
00:31:46,696 --> 00:31:48,655
- And you believe him?
- Of course not.

569
00:31:48,823 --> 00:31:51,366
It's a transparent con.
Q-Tip killed them all right.

570
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:55,120
Carris is just trying to save his skin
by laying the blame elsewhere.

571
00:31:55,288 --> 00:31:56,872
On your father probably.

572
00:31:57,040 --> 00:32:00,125
He must've known about
his connection to Patrice.

573
00:32:00,293 --> 00:32:03,253
So we're gonna play along.
Let the shooter come to us.

574
00:32:03,421 --> 00:32:05,547
Carris has set up a meeting
with Q-Tip tonight.

575
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:09,468
So we'll grab up Q-Tip and work him
till we get the real story.

576
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:11,887
So, uh, what do you need me for exactly?

577
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:16,350
If this is gonna work, I can't have
a whole bunch of angry Davis PD's...

578
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:18,769
...swarming all over Carris and his crew.

579
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:22,022
And the CBI is kind of unpopular
with you guys right now.

580
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:23,231
Yes, you are.

581
00:32:23,399 --> 00:32:27,235
So we were hoping you'd have
a quiet word with your chief...

582
00:32:27,403 --> 00:32:29,613
...let him know what we're up to.

583
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:32,366
Knowing the chief,
he's gonna wanna know the details.

584
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:34,993
When and where you're gonna be
meeting this Q-Tip...

585
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:37,913
...and what personnel you got
operating undercover.

586
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:41,416
Sure. But this needs to stay close
between you and the chief.

587
00:32:41,584 --> 00:32:43,001
We don't wanna spook Carris.

588
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:46,880
He thinks he's playing us
for a bunch of idiots.

589
00:32:47,423 --> 00:32:48,465
I understand.

590
00:33:10,905 --> 00:33:13,532
Okay, team. Let the games begin.

591
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:14,741
Carris is on his way.

592
00:33:14,909 --> 00:33:17,953
He's gonna call when he meets
with Q-Tip. Be ready to act fast.

593
00:33:18,121 --> 00:33:19,329
Clear?

594
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:23,583
- Got it.
- Okay.

595
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,877
Roger that.

596
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:38,098
The warehouse is on Fifth and Geary.
Loading dock in the back.

597
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:41,101
Q-Tip's in the car he was on the tape.
California plate...

598
00:33:41,269 --> 00:33:44,187
...Five-Nora-Tom-Queen-nine-five-seven.

599
00:33:44,355 --> 00:33:46,606
- Be there in 10 minutes.
- Ten? I can't get...

600
00:33:46,774 --> 00:33:50,193
- ...to Fifth and Geary in 10 minutes.
- Well, do your best.

601
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:57,534
On our way.
ETA to Geary and Fifth, 12 minutes.

602
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:03,749
Damn it. He won't wait that long.

603
00:34:08,004 --> 00:34:11,465
Officer Blakely?
Are you closer to Fifth and Geary?

604
00:34:15,386 --> 00:34:17,971
Officer Blakely? Sam?

605
00:35:01,015 --> 00:35:02,974
- Blakely, drop the gun!
- Drop it!

606
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:24,621
Carris never made a deal, did he?

607
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:26,331
No.

608
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:29,501
We, uh, edited the surveillance footage.

609
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:33,839
Q-Tip was just some guy that happened
to walk up to the motel at some point.

610
00:35:34,006 --> 00:35:38,176
And, uh, Van Pelt, she laid in
the license plate with Photoshop.

611
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:42,055
It's clever. Kudos to you guys.

612
00:35:42,223 --> 00:35:44,057
We know you're a decent man, Sam.

613
00:35:44,225 --> 00:35:46,810
We know you didn't mean for things
to go down like this.

614
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:49,604
- Just tell us what happened.
- I got nothing to say.

615
00:35:50,231 --> 00:35:54,109
- There's no use in hiding anything now.
- There's no use in explaining it either.

616
00:36:01,117 --> 00:36:03,160
- Take a seat, detective.
- Okay.

617
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:10,500
- Son.
- Dad.

618
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:16,882
There's always a reckoning.

619
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:19,593
This is it.

620
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:22,721
Just tell them the truth.

621
00:36:22,930 --> 00:36:24,598
The truth, huh?

622
00:36:25,057 --> 00:36:27,100
Tell the truth no matter what.

623
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,561
That's the mark of a man, right, Dad?

624
00:36:29,729 --> 00:36:33,273
Tell the truth. A man has his honor
and his word and that's it.

625
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:35,609
Don't go over the same ground
for God's sake.

626
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:38,486
- Just give them the facts.
- You want the facts? Okay.

627
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:40,697
Mom suspected
that Dad was having an affair.

628
00:36:41,282 --> 00:36:43,116
Well, I asked around on the street...

629
00:36:43,284 --> 00:36:45,869
...pretty soon I hear
that he's keeping this girl...

630
00:36:46,037 --> 00:36:48,914
...Patrice Matigan, on the side.

631
00:36:50,791 --> 00:36:52,918
I was mad as hell.

632
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:57,088
You gotta understand, this integrity crap
was banged into me my entire life.

633
00:36:57,256 --> 00:36:58,757
Right, Dad?

634
00:36:58,925 --> 00:37:01,760
Honesty. Honor. Family.
Banged into me.

635
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:05,722
And then all this time he's keeping
a whore on the side? No, never.

636
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:07,807
I went and I asked him if it was true...

637
00:37:08,935 --> 00:37:10,644
...and he said no.

638
00:37:10,978 --> 00:37:15,023
I knew he was lying to me. I knew it.

639
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:19,110
So Sunday night,
I went back to find the truth.

640
00:37:20,905 --> 00:37:22,822
I thought for sure
she was gonna meet Dad.

641
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:26,910
And she went to the store, went to a motel.

642
00:37:29,455 --> 00:37:32,582
I thought, "Ah-ha, I got him now."

643
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:47,555
Purcell must have thought
I'd been sent by Carris to kill him.

644
00:37:47,723 --> 00:37:49,975
I had no choice.

645
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:02,821
I panicked.

646
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:05,073
I drove away.

647
00:38:07,368 --> 00:38:09,828
Then Dispatch called.

648
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:12,247
Sent me right back to the motel.

649
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:15,834
I was the closest unit.
What was I gonna do? Refuse the call?

650
00:38:17,211 --> 00:38:19,045
I had to take it.

651
00:38:24,593 --> 00:38:27,345
So was it reckoning?

652
00:38:27,513 --> 00:38:30,307
Patrice wasn't your mistress, was she?

653
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:33,810
No.

654
00:38:37,231 --> 00:38:39,232
She was my daughter.

655
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:41,693
Sam's sister.

656
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:43,945
How did you know?

657
00:38:44,613 --> 00:38:47,574
Sam told his mother
you weren't cheating on her.

658
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:49,117
I believed him.

659
00:38:49,285 --> 00:38:50,785
But then who was Patrice?

660
00:38:52,246 --> 00:38:54,331
Who was she to you?

661
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:55,749
And why all the secrecy?

662
00:38:55,916 --> 00:38:58,585
I just figured
she had to have been your daughter.

663
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:02,630
I never knew Patrice existed
until four years ago.

664
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:05,633
Her mother was dying...

665
00:39:07,303 --> 00:39:08,887
...so she got in touch.

666
00:39:10,222 --> 00:39:15,935
Told me I had a 16-year-old child
I never knew about.

667
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:19,522
Blew my mind. It just...

668
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,610
Oh, it blew my mind.

669
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:27,030
Yeah, I wanted to tell Katherine
the truth...

670
00:39:29,450 --> 00:39:31,618
...but, you know, I...

671
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:34,996
Oh, my God.

672
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:38,583
I couldn't do it.

673
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:43,088
I just couldn't hurt her like that.

674
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:45,090
- Does she know now?
- Yeah.

675
00:39:45,257 --> 00:39:46,883
She knows.

676
00:39:47,802 --> 00:39:49,969
She knows.

677
00:40:37,017 --> 00:40:38,601
Sorry. Busy right now.

678
00:40:38,769 --> 00:40:42,272
Katherine, it's Patrick Jane.
Can you open the door?

679
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,942
- I can't.
- You can and you will.

680
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:47,819
I have something I need to give you.

681
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:57,620
This is Kaylee, your granddaughter,
kind of.

682
00:40:57,788 --> 00:40:59,122
Here.

683
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:03,084
She's very fond of Cheerios.

684
00:41:03,252 --> 00:41:06,588
That has nothing to do with me.
She likes to take her big nap at 2.

685
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:09,007
- But... What?
- You're all she has.

686
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:13,428
Social Services will be along later
to get the paperwork signed.

687
00:41:13,596 --> 00:41:16,264
I think Kaylee doesn't really suit her,
if you ask me.

688
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:19,184
If you wanna change it,
I'm sure no one will make a fuss.

689
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:21,895
Oh, oh, hey. You might need those.

690
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:24,189
Bye.

